{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100503","id":2239180797,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Fdy_9","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100503","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100503.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100503.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100503","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100503/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100503/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100503/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/1810135f4b5ba17587ca250ad545a9b493f59e7f","number":100503,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Scene Shaders - Vertex Shading Fixes","user":{"login":"StaydMcMuffin","id":38304659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MzA0NjU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38304659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin","html_url":"https://github.com/StaydMcMuffin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/StaydMcMuffin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Part three of: #100348\r\nRequires the preceding: #100441\r\n\r\nAddresses ~~six~~ five errors found in the scene shader files that relate to per-vertex shading.\r\n\r\n- In **Forward+** and **Compatibility**, the geometry normals used for per-vertex shading were not normalized prior to their use, causing per-vertex shading to be either too bright or too dark depending on the overall scale of the model matrix. Specular shading in particular was _strongly_ affected by this.\r\n\r\n- For per-vertex shading specifically, the **Lambert Wrap** diffuse model mistakenly used the clamped `cNdotL` rather than the signed `NdotL`, meaning it could not, in fact, wrap.\r\n\r\n- Per-vertex shading completely ignored both the contributing lights' `specular_amount` and `size` parameters.\r\n\r\n- ~~Per-vertex specularity lacked a Geometry term entirely, resulting in overly bright rough highlights and a generally different \"look\" compared to per-pixel shading. It now uses the same approximate G term used for clearcoat specular.\r\nThis may be considered as much of an improvement as it is a fix, but it's a fairly innocent one at that.~~\r\nDropped for performance.\r\n\r\n- The `roughness_to_shininess` mapping from GGX roughness to Blinn-Phong shininess used for per-vertex shading resulted in very different specular responses between per-pixel and per-vertex shading, generally making materials look far more glossy despite having the same roughness. I've replaced it with a new formulation entirely, which loosely follows the curve of the common `2 / roughness * roughness - 2` remapping, but with a much lower maximum value more suitable for per-vertex shading.\r\n\r\n- Per-vertex shading incorrectly used the unmodified Blinn-Phong normalization term `(shininess + 2.0) / (8.0 * PI)` as opposed to the modified one `(shininess + 8.0) / (8.0 * PI)` (the modified term is the one you want when multiplying by `NdotL`).\r\n\r\nHere is a swatch of roughness values, from `0.0` on the left to `1.0` on the right in intervals of `0.2`. The top row uses per-pixel shading while the bottom uses per-vertex.\r\n| Before | After |\r\n|--------|--------|\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/53436f03-9e21-4647-8a8d-1c266d748a44) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cd89a7a5-14c3-40f4-9b23-7439db2d47c0) |\r\n\r\nHere is a material tester using per-vertex shading with the Lambert Wrap diffuse mode and a roughness of `0.4`. The mesh also has a uniform scale of `0.8`, which causes the specularity to disappear completely in the \"Before\" image.\r\n| Before | After | Per-pixel |\r\n|--------|--------|--------|\r\n| ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3f12f0a-1a7e-4a5c-afd7-522b878835f3) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7ee6fdd-0814-4399-86df-8cce3390cfad) | ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ae714f87-65c0-4807-b8bc-711c3e1e5209) |","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godot